values ('e0f1a2b3-4c5d-4f00-9a90-1b2c3d4e5f00', 'sociological-research-methods', 'Sociological Research Methods', 'Students learn how sociologists turn social problems into researchable questions that can be answered with evidence, and how methods connect to sociological theory, prior scholarship, conceptual models, and explicit expectations about social patterns. The course covers study design, measurement, sampling, surveys, causal inference, quantitative analysis, interviewing, fieldwork, content and computational analysis, comparative-historical methods, mixed methods and research transparency, ethics with vulnerable communities and sensitive data, and a capstone study proposal.');

