  'Sociological Research Methods',
  'Students learn how sociologists turn social problems into researchable questions that can be answered with evidence, and how methods connect to sociological theory, prior scholarship, conceptual models, and explicit expectations about social patterns. The course covers study design, measurement, sampling, surveys, causal inference, quantitative analysis, interviewing, fieldwork, content and computational analysis, comparative-historical methods, mixed methods and research transparency, ethics with vulnerable communities and sensitive data, and a capstone study proposal.',
  $srmjson${"slug": "sociological-research-methods", "title": "Sociological Research Methods", "description": "Students learn how sociologists turn social problems into researchable questions that can be answered with evidence, and how methods connect to sociological theory, prior scholarship, conceptual models, and explicit expectations about social patterns. The course covers study design, measurement, sampling, surveys, causal inference, quantitative analysis, interviewing, fieldwork, content and computational analysis, comparative-historical methods, mixed methods and research transparency, ethics with vulnerable communities and sensitive data, and a capstone study proposal.", "topics": [{"id": "1e3c0671-6fe8-44db-a81f-b2d795242f42", "type": "topic", "title": "Sociological Inquiry, Research Questions, and the Logic of Evidence", "description": "Students begin by learning how sociologists turn social problems into researchable questions that can be answered with evidence.", "children": [{"id": "a0f56a9e-1bec-4507-8f5f-76e2bf9df4fb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sociological questions", "children": [{"id": "534a4c97-9a58-4257-bf3d-4d0a4e870754", "type": "concept", "title": "Descriptive, explanatory, interpretive, evaluative, and causal questions"}, {"id": "cd88b342-e531-4457-b933-b60c017f9477", "type": "concept", "title": "Scope, population, setting, time, and level of analysis"}, {"id": "9232d4bb-65ff-478e-a032-51a6d7ed63be", "type": "concept", "title": "Feasibility, significance, and contribution"}], "description": "Students learn that strong methods begin with precise questions about social patterns, meanings, institutions, and change."}, {"id": "0513747e-00ab-4824-8b5f-b7c85ecb2c7b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evidence and inference", "children": [{"id": "8e885fce-2046-4195-8e45-6a444b1ab11a", "type": "concept", "title": "Data, evidence, argument, and inference"}, {"id": "c84cf3db-6201-4328-971c-f7c12a18678c", "type": "concept", "title": "Description, interpretation, prediction, and explanation"}, {"id": "f8779386-a976-4d54-a4bc-f12a00e08d8b", "type": "concept", "title": "Alternative explanations and rival hypotheses"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces the basic chain from observation to claim."}, {"id": "5e8db1ab-bb61-4299-b4e5-92a89ff2d66c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "The sociological imagination as method", "children": [{"id": "c9da4477-a55c-4d0a-9c73-ac448595f6b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Linking biography and structure"}, {"id": "543e8f39-821a-4a9f-a138-87ecfdc0efd4", "type": "concept", "title": "Micro, meso, and macro levels"}, {"id": "7925a9bb-9f53-41bc-a687-adb01023021f", "type": "concept", "title": "Institutions, inequality, culture, and social change as research contexts"}], "description": "Students connect personal troubles, public issues, and empirical evidence."}]}, {"id": "88c0304b-42a3-4d47-af8c-9577753a09e8", "type": "topic", "title": "Theory, Literature Reviews, Conceptual Frameworks, and Hypothesis Building", "description": "This topic connects methods to sociological theory, prior scholarship, conceptual models, and explicit expectations about social patterns.", "children": [{"id": "190080ad-7ded-4c98-a68a-71854b53e94a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Using theory in research", "children": [{"id": "3a209342-b3ff-4fa8-8cd6-682097df5200", "type": "concept", "title": "Functionalist, conflict, interactionist, feminist, critical, and network perspectives"}, {"id": "c78c8487-782c-434b-84e6-0607412c49d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Deductive and inductive reasoning"}, {"id": "c1f85239-7b13-47e9-a9d7-189347678b32", "type": "concept", "title": "Theory as lens, mechanism, and explanation"}], "description": "Students learn how theory guides what to look for, how to explain it, and what counts as evidence."}, {"id": "87cb054f-7b34-41f7-a4eb-2441da6c7884", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Literature review strategy", "children": [{"id": "a8bb7d76-0154-494e-9c82-3ae769fcb272", "type": "concept", "title": "Search terms, databases, citation chaining, and source evaluation"}, {"id": "a8c62300-47ee-4966-90e7-144504d7658e", "type": "concept", "title": "Synthesizing rather than listing sources"}, {"id": "155cab3e-9e1f-4e5b-a313-55086de688e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Identifying gaps, debates, and unresolved puzzles"}], "description": "This subtopic teaches students to place a project inside an existing scholarly conversation."}, {"id": "c165cb42-dd9e-4b04-a47f-714295180f61", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Conceptual frameworks and hypotheses", "children": [{"id": "de97179c-7163-41e8-aeac-e7727b665c18", "type": "concept", "title": "Concept maps, mechanisms, and variables"}, {"id": "f30f743b-a159-4858-9992-af7ef068d5c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Hypotheses and propositions"}, {"id": "3d41f063-c208-4a69-acef-8d1646ab2f1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Boundary conditions and assumptions"}], "description": "Students translate theory and literature into a coherent model of expectations."}]}, {"id": "dcc65e84-a2a1-467c-a789-ebda141c7060", "type": "topic", "title": "Research Design: Units of Analysis, Cases, Comparisons, Time, and Validity", "description": "Students learn to design studies that match questions, evidence, cases, time frames, and claims.", "children": [{"id": "305ba7c2-b766-4df4-b588-cbb3a722e318", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Design alignment", "children": [{"id": "753ebe1f-6730-46e9-aeb6-f47d4c7ff964", "type": "concept", "title": "Research design matrix"}, {"id": "7634d66d-1670-4522-a8af-5e975d992737", "type": "concept", "title": "Unit of analysis vs unit of observation"}, {"id": "9b7fdf63-5ed0-4048-85ab-7d1e7a64a028", "type": "concept", "title": "Choosing cases, sites, populations, and evidence"}], "description": "Students learn to align question, theory, data, method, and claim."}, {"id": "9c882935-9fab-4af9-be60-ccbfb22792a5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comparison and time", "children": [{"id": "8f9e2c1e-95c0-4898-b49b-ece12e1419b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-sectional, longitudinal, panel, and retrospective designs"}, {"id": "5b7dede0-be52-4afc-91bf-7c0a34a3b8ad", "type": "concept", "title": "Most-similar and most-different comparisons"}, {"id": "91dc2994-406f-411e-bdda-90e8a86dda9c", "type": "concept", "title": "Case selection and comparative logic"}], "description": "This subtopic covers how sociologists study difference, sequence, and change."}, {"id": "ce05bd2f-77c8-4ef3-84a1-158cc97c14f4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Validity and credibility", "children": [{"id": "a12d45a6-8ea5-4956-85f8-5fa557cb2fa5", "type": "concept", "title": "Internal, external, construct, ecological, and statistical validity"}, {"id": "5c42ce22-4587-4588-95aa-26a08b109058", "type": "concept", "title": "Credibility, transferability, dependability, and confirmability"}, {"id": "1e53b098-702d-474e-84f2-f0077bb93512", "type": "concept", "title": "Threats, tradeoffs, and design limitations"}], "description": "Students learn to evaluate whether a design can support the claims it makes."}]}, {"id": "61b61b44-460a-4a93-a182-c98554cd145b", "type": "topic", "title": "Conceptualization, Operationalization, Measurement, Reliability, and Validity", "description": "This section teaches students how abstract sociological concepts become measurable, observable, and interpretable indicators.", "children": [{"id": "cc2006fa-adac-44ef-9828-cdbf35889203", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Conceptualization", "children": [{"id": "65ad570f-216d-4d78-8c01-e3952c8f7e2f", "type": "concept", "title": "Poverty, class, race, gender, power, stigma, trust, social capital, and belonging"}, {"id": "11980758-e516-4453-88bb-a9e9b2f2c86b", "type": "concept", "title": "Dimensions and indicators"}, {"id": "985d41c5-079a-4b2d-a558-3f445cdbcf39", "type": "concept", "title": "Concept stretching and context"}], "description": "Students learn to define abstract sociological concepts clearly before measuring them."}, {"id": "35f2895e-7c7f-47eb-8c6d-71a060939602", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Operationalization and measurement", "children": [{"id": "69074aab-d0cb-43a1-ab84-bc078e6f0787", "type": "concept", "title": "Survey items, scales, indexes, codes, and administrative indicators"}, {"id": "f88ef291-372b-49df-9b2c-8a12c6c1dfa6", "type": "concept", "title": "Nominal, ordinal, interval, and ratio measurement"}, {"id": "2f077554-8a95-428c-a8cc-1bd01217fb11", "type": "concept", "title": "Measurement error and missingness"}], "description": "This subtopic turns concepts into observable evidence."}, {"id": "58a55b0d-c4ab-47b7-b551-2406e90ddf0e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reliability and validity", "children": [{"id": "31a56154-f26c-4421-8afd-a4b7666a8fe6", "type": "concept", "title": "Intercoder reliability and internal consistency"}, {"id": "52e58920-2392-4149-a196-b10d92986626", "type": "concept", "title": "Face, content, criterion, and construct validity"}, {"id": "3f73bbb1-202b-4786-9303-eeb768b228c3", "type": "concept", "title": "Measurement equivalence across groups"}], "description": "Students evaluate whether measures are consistent and meaningful."}]}, {"id": "5365368a-887b-4f05-ba64-a6c16828c998", "type": "topic", "title": "Sampling, Recruitment, Representativeness, Power, and Field Access", "description": "Students examine how researchers select people, sites, texts, organizations, events, and datasets while managing feasibility and bias.", "children": [{"id": "4b556e89-b104-4579-8740-2bd10d734888", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sampling logic", "children": [{"id": "41b1a230-ddf8-4d0d-9543-eb7066c7136a", "type": "concept", "title": "Population, sampling frame, sample, and cases"}, {"id": "f690ecf5-f848-42ec-8dc7-9715689eccd6", "type": "concept", "title": "Probability and nonprobability sampling"}, {"id": "0ca37f34-e8dc-41fd-824c-5acb7972045f", "type": "concept", "title": "Representativeness, saturation, and theoretical sampling"}], "description": "Students learn how sampling decisions shape what can be claimed."}, {"id": "91785f42-cb12-4662-80d3-ec61a3871841", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Recruitment and access", "children": [{"id": "93ff2c5a-784c-4a7a-9bb3-9056581e3e7f", "type": "concept", "title": "Gatekeepers, permissions, incentives, and trust"}, {"id": "7f262d29-128b-4118-bc57-67c9047cac3f", "type": "concept", "title": "Hard-to-reach and vulnerable populations"}, {"id": "a656b148-e7bd-4fe0-8798-f323cf18a61f", "type": "concept", "title": "Response rates, attrition, and refusal"}], "description": "This subtopic prepares students for the practical and relational work of research."}, {"id": "4bc0a482-4656-4aec-bf10-e991bda19271", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sample size and power", "children": [{"id": "60404ae3-f5a2-4793-ad81-94fa4e4915b7", "type": "concept", "title": "Power analysis basics"}, {"id": "851c5022-68b1-4df5-b029-9f684616a45b", "type": "concept", "title": "Precision, uncertainty, and subgroup analysis"}, {"id": "f5ebb852-ae52-4ebc-8b74-7bc3a644b582", "type": "concept", "title": "Qualitative depth, saturation, and information power"}], "description": "Students learn to justify sample sizes for both qualitative and quantitative projects."}]}, {"id": "697647f8-c578-4017-8663-a4f91253f4f1", "type": "topic", "title": "Survey Research and Questionnaire Design", "description": "This topic develops the skills needed to design, administer, analyze, and critique surveys as sociological evidence.", "children": [{"id": "3d0ce8c4-1e78-4510-befb-bfb3b791e0e9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Survey design", "children": [{"id": "c5920bff-f642-4a0c-b057-0e4371752b69", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-sectional and panel surveys"}, {"id": "7938ea83-c92f-48f7-b6a2-eb62e32372e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Modes: online, phone, mail, face-to-face, and mixed-mode"}, {"id": "932638a3-9fbd-45a1-bbf1-9ea29f97b972", "type": "concept", "title": "Public opinion, attitudes, behavior, identity, and demographics"}], "description": "Students learn when surveys are useful and what they can and cannot show."}, {"id": "25620771-e901-4532-92e8-fce74fc6dd71", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Questionnaire construction", "children": [{"id": "7651155e-fff7-4d1a-87d8-0d84b8467050", "type": "concept", "title": "Question wording, order effects, response options, and scales"}, {"id": "4a2a1b67-e3e9-4579-93d3-cd1cea538149", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensitive questions and social desirability bias"}, {"id": "ba9e5a73-4448-43f1-9b14-80ab2cf9869b", "type": "concept", "title": "Pilot testing and cognitive interviewing"}], "description": "This subtopic teaches students to design clear, ethical, and analyzable questions."}, {"id": "0f635e94-49a2-4748-92f5-80f2672a5486", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Survey analysis and transparency", "children": [{"id": "5611b0d5-9c6d-4dba-8dab-992e2a4d03d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Weights, margins of error, and uncertainty"}, {"id": "6c6f1885-ec84-4bf6-a47f-feca25c9b25b", "type": "concept", "title": "Nonresponse and coverage error"}, {"id": "9b357cb4-beaa-4425-be4a-a3c2ecceae8b", "type": "concept", "title": "Methods reports and reproducible codebooks"}], "description": "Students learn how survey evidence depends on sampling, weighting, and disclosure."}]}, {"id": "f651decf-414c-44ca-a8c9-c4644d0b1f31", "type": "topic", "title": "Experimental, Quasi-Experimental, and Causal Inference Designs", "description": "Students learn the logic of causal claims and the strengths and limits of experiments, natural experiments, and observational causal designs.", "children": [{"id": "61a509ad-158d-4328-9487-71637d906e15", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Causal logic", "children": [{"id": "5a001a5b-e1fb-4d54-9144-6fdabf2204b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Counterfactuals and potential outcomes"}, {"id": "58f1c41d-2e16-4150-b957-5a485efc86ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Confounding, selection bias, and omitted variables"}, {"id": "2a1168f7-7ef9-479a-92d9-cd760c665c1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Mediators, moderators, and mechanisms"}], "description": "Students learn the difference between association and causation."}, {"id": "a387227b-dfab-4cfe-9495-eedcb6260c02", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Experimental designs", "children": [{"id": "a41f8116-7b51-4f5b-ba9b-a7cd409af03f", "type": "concept", "title": "Lab, survey, field, and audit experiments"}, {"id": "1626b962-3492-44c5-97b9-d4dbf7615264", "type": "concept", "title": "Random assignment, treatment, control, and manipulation checks"}, {"id": "02350ba5-69ac-46a3-bdea-ad6475ca337d", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethics and external validity"}], "description": "This subtopic covers randomized designs and their sociological uses."}, {"id": "6a8a45e5-2652-4f31-b4b0-7cec94068872", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Quasi-experimental designs", "children": [{"id": "f974f37e-9be6-482e-9f09-4c8f479f854e", "type": "concept", "title": "Natural experiments and difference-in-differences"}, {"id": "5a010033-9a68-4c4e-bda1-0b1e9df82dc2", "type": "concept", "title": "Regression discontinuity and instrumental variables"}, {"id": "daf57eba-3308-477f-a974-74ed17876e3d", "type": "concept", "title": "Matching, fixed effects, and causal limits"}], "description": "Students learn alternatives when randomization is impossible."}]}, {"id": "72fe7485-d997-4a24-968b-d7d35561be15", "type": "topic", "title": "Quantitative Data Analysis, Visualization, and Statistical Inference", "description": "This section builds practical fluency with descriptive statistics, uncertainty, group comparison, regression, visualization, and interpretation.", "children": [{"id": "bd935de3-83b2-440c-86e7-d79a6a877ee5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Descriptive statistics and visualization", "children": [{"id": "b4e305c9-5ce7-4638-bd7e-d68e6205349c", "type": "concept", "title": "Distributions, central tendency, variation, and cross-tabulation"}, {"id": "ef621aca-09ed-441e-8c67-7ed1289ec0aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Rates, proportions, indexes, and standardized comparisons"}, {"id": "93f950ae-8fa3-4594-86dc-98aa3f8bc5c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Tables, charts, maps, and clear labels"}], "description": "Students learn to summarize and display social patterns responsibly."}, {"id": "439abaf4-0524-4cb9-829a-a4406f9e2511", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inference and uncertainty", "children": [{"id": "d7ba2b76-37df-4b7b-9e6f-22ec85aa5070", "type": "concept", "title": "Standard errors, confidence intervals, and hypothesis tests"}, {"id": "2076314e-a877-4303-937e-5e4440d79cb7", "type": "concept", "title": "Group comparisons, correlation, and regression"}, {"id": "e2734b39-df44-421a-85cb-ce7f97bfc61b", "type": "concept", "title": "Effect sizes and practical significance"}], "description": "This subtopic explains how researchers reason from samples to broader claims."}, {"id": "1cd8f161-23ee-49b7-8523-e328f9d74896", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data cleaning and reproducibility", "children": [{"id": "73149872-f6df-4125-a56c-2575f7d5bee2", "type": "concept", "title": "Data dictionaries, recoding, missing data, and outliers"}, {"id": "02023bd1-0fc4-4968-b3b3-e597d3b257fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Reproducible scripts and version control basics"}, {"id": "5705c2a4-3cfe-4dfa-8caf-e2984b3c679d", "type": "concept", "title": "Documenting choices and sensitivity checks"}], "description": "Students practice research workflows that can be checked by others."}]}, {"id": "2ec7df26-93b6-4ccf-8e22-9c726752e1f3", "type": "topic", "title": "Interviewing, Focus Groups, and Qualitative Design", "description": "Students learn how qualitative interviewing produces rich evidence about meaning, experience, institutions, and social processes.", "children": [{"id": "66f67c8f-c232-427d-a076-22d1a082199d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interview design", "children": [{"id": "9eff217f-4069-4728-85f4-62d8f5e634a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Structured, semi-structured, and unstructured interviews"}, {"id": "05f2e91a-a87c-4208-96a7-36f0772ee71d", "type": "concept", "title": "Interview guides and probes"}, {"id": "cf175bdf-297d-491c-b96c-b47375ed25b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Rapport, positionality, and power"}], "description": "Students learn how interviews reveal meanings, narratives, identities, and institutional experiences."}, {"id": "42469dbb-952f-4347-9f04-fea8885e2978", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Focus groups", "children": [{"id": "847c658e-d795-4f10-bb1e-6355bc68b486", "type": "concept", "title": "Group composition and facilitation"}, {"id": "daf1b328-c7bc-4c57-899c-e0c76e2c4473", "type": "concept", "title": "Consensus, disagreement, and social norms"}, {"id": "8b9539c6-00c7-44ef-95af-f7a8f8bf4956", "type": "concept", "title": "Managing sensitive topics and dominant voices"}], "description": "This subtopic teaches how group interaction can itself become data."}, {"id": "7447efc8-c591-4734-87f2-0d3e920444b3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Qualitative analysis", "children": [{"id": "f9d5ee68-ecc0-4202-ad94-38422185c3ef", "type": "concept", "title": "Open, axial, thematic, and analytic coding"}, {"id": "8ae2f6a1-3666-411e-8f00-e6fe91144a77", "type": "concept", "title": "Memos, codebooks, and matrices"}, {"id": "7fe3c944-86bd-4c89-9d76-78c9cdeacd18", "type": "concept", "title": "Negative cases and analytic saturation"}], "description": "Students learn to move from transcripts to credible interpretations."}]}, {"id": "1f400e3e-7746-4fb0-8707-0fb18070ff4d", "type": "topic", "title": "Ethnography, Field Research, Observation, and Reflexive Fieldnotes", "description": "This topic centers fieldwork as a way to understand social life in context through observation, participation, relationships, and reflexivity.", "children": [{"id": "af11abcc-11d0-49e0-9210-093023f83a4d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethnographic orientation", "children": [{"id": "01d1601e-c9ad-4c15-848c-1095a13d3738", "type": "concept", "title": "Participant observation and nonparticipant observation"}, {"id": "1af29cc6-4dee-4b81-982a-99dfa03dbcf9", "type": "concept", "title": "Sites, scenes, routines, interactions, and artifacts"}, {"id": "ec234c9d-a528-4e4f-86db-23b247162190", "type": "concept", "title": "Thick description and immersion"}], "description": "Students learn how fieldwork studies social life in context."}, {"id": "8e675b36-3640-4864-9905-1d25252b7261", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fieldnotes and reflexivity", "children": [{"id": "da7fd6d2-7e11-4e6f-853a-399095a5c906", "type": "concept", "title": "Jottings, expanded notes, analytic memos, and fieldnote structure"}, {"id": "5c5c1219-241a-4339-9d0f-2c070f26e3b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Researcher role, positionality, and reactivity"}, {"id": "252bf5aa-f045-4525-b6fe-54662cb3e60c", "type": "concept", "title": "Access, rapport, and boundary management"}], "description": "This subtopic emphasizes disciplined observation and self-awareness."}, {"id": "de8dd3bc-75f1-4401-a67c-764bfc126b04", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fieldwork analysis and ethics", "children": [{"id": "9816b355-8d27-467d-ba4a-2f4768f9ef71", "type": "concept", "title": "Patterns, events, sequences, and grounded claims"}, {"id": "133dfb51-0c40-49f9-9dc9-b7dfd77b537f", "type": "concept", "title": "Confidentiality in small communities"}, {"id": "91bb006e-3d6e-493b-a49c-08a1165c1c40", "type": "concept", "title": "Exit, reciprocity, and representation"}], "description": "Students learn to interpret field evidence responsibly."}]}, {"id": "11386081-b900-4136-ae2b-4dbd640d3167", "type": "topic", "title": "Content Analysis, Digital Trace Data, Text, Media, and Computational Sociology", "description": "Students analyze cultural materials, media, documents, online traces, and texts as sociological data.", "children": [{"id": "1e5b0d97-4aa2-44c4-9a2c-d4ea5df08b80", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Content analysis", "children": [{"id": "e45da614-61df-4252-b41b-3faacc3d3592", "type": "concept", "title": "Sampling texts, images, posts, documents, and media"}, {"id": "f1f2bb25-0302-47b1-a708-ff1007e89451", "type": "concept", "title": "Manifest and latent content"}, {"id": "5565ed52-3210-4f02-9071-64f0fd69baab", "type": "concept", "title": "Codebooks, intercoder reliability, and examples"}], "description": "Students learn to study meanings, frames, symbols, and representation systematically."}, {"id": "ede101b6-885b-42ba-b202-04362ff9e197", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital trace data", "children": [{"id": "5a80d97b-5e12-4b7b-a07d-e710553967f0", "type": "concept", "title": "Social media, web archives, administrative logs, and metadata"}, {"id": "3f78025e-8361-4c35-b5ef-05c06ee8be9c", "type": "concept", "title": "APIs, scraping, terms of service, and access limits"}, {"id": "2d8655a5-f4a7-4326-8d97-4a97402b9f88", "type": "concept", "title": "Bias, missingness, platform effects, and ethics"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces data generated by platforms, devices, archives, and online activity."}, {"id": "f783ac1e-4b80-4465-b2ae-84adef84f0d5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Text and computational approaches", "children": [{"id": "1fef187a-5593-4299-b139-99376bfd36ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Keyword, dictionary, topic, network, and sentiment approaches"}, {"id": "cb416e2f-8aaa-416f-935c-3f67c1273df2", "type": "concept", "title": "Annotation and validation"}, {"id": "d9ef0e16-b32a-44f2-b4b5-9899cbc8a202", "type": "concept", "title": "Interpretability, fairness, and contextual reading"}], "description": "Students see how computational tools can extend but not replace sociological interpretation."}]}, {"id": "4ce64906-c5b7-4e50-9c5f-6b23ae9b0652", "type": "topic", "title": "Comparative-Historical Methods, Case Studies, and Process Tracing", "description": "This section teaches students how to study social change, institutions, and causal processes across cases and over time.", "children": [{"id": "d21e5182-4c27-4ac8-8f1d-8fb433d1bd08", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comparative-historical reasoning", "children": [{"id": "28b24150-2280-4873-b5f7-e1e4c09e6df9", "type": "concept", "title": "State formation, revolutions, welfare regimes, migration, race, and capitalism"}, {"id": "4129e623-f169-4535-a022-2802313fa8dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Archival evidence and historical datasets"}, {"id": "747842c8-ac1b-45c7-ac52-acb06304e9de", "type": "concept", "title": "Sequence, path dependence, and contingency"}], "description": "Students learn to study large social processes across time and place."}, {"id": "d4b47134-ba57-4461-bbed-83dc6089c642", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Case study design", "children": [{"id": "d4105428-2d1b-4568-a086-95b69b625818", "type": "concept", "title": "Typical, deviant, extreme, crucial, and comparative cases"}, {"id": "36e73d01-3536-4408-9c79-b5b289eac9b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Within-case and cross-case analysis"}, {"id": "3bb03f92-7c4f-4aaa-91dd-8fb1979f19bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Generalization and transferability"}], "description": "This subtopic teaches students how to choose and justify cases."}, {"id": "09135e00-50ec-4aa4-b431-771183cd7176", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Process tracing", "children": [{"id": "6da0cb64-a952-4196-9491-b4715850d745", "type": "concept", "title": "Timelines, events, mechanisms, and evidence tests"}, {"id": "ee31e77b-0150-4da5-8a91-05d59f29cb4f", "type": "concept", "title": "Hoop tests and smoking-gun evidence"}, {"id": "300e0c6d-ed2f-4bcd-b619-b11409316e6e", "type": "concept", "title": "Alternative explanations and causal narratives"}], "description": "Students learn how to evaluate mechanisms and causal sequences."}]}, {"id": "645ced2f-dfb0-4e2b-ac3a-9e764920b236", "type": "topic", "title": "Mixed Methods, Triangulation, Replication, and Research Transparency", "description": "Students learn how to integrate multiple forms of evidence while making research workflows transparent, reproducible, and credible.", "children": [{"id": "e2e0830a-90c2-46e5-b1eb-4ecd69a5301e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mixed-methods designs", "children": [{"id": "f47d7a98-5ce7-4fce-8407-6a8912d465a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Sequential, convergent, embedded, and explanatory designs"}, {"id": "51da4713-0c20-43cd-8bf8-569d418e73a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Connecting sampling, instruments, and findings"}, {"id": "460e8214-b126-4c6d-be27-d021436d3bb3", "type": "concept", "title": "Integration points and design tradeoffs"}], "description": "Students learn why and how to integrate qualitative and quantitative evidence."}, {"id": "ab467a9d-6037-4344-9cb4-8771287e3aa8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Triangulation and robustness", "children": [{"id": "b1080381-68f5-4f15-abb9-0b4cef2df188", "type": "concept", "title": "Data, method, theory, and investigator triangulation"}, {"id": "aa737a4a-e717-4716-9c50-5b1efd221c8c", "type": "concept", "title": "Robustness checks and sensitivity analysis"}, {"id": "2be3cb52-01f5-41ee-bdee-9bfb29ea0804", "type": "concept", "title": "Contradictory evidence and explanation"}], "description": "This subtopic shows how multiple sources can strengthen or complicate claims."}, {"id": "ef9a2d42-600f-4c9e-8d8e-29cea2e45cfb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Open and transparent research", "children": [{"id": "a476f10d-f66e-4038-992b-7ec61bccc49f", "type": "concept", "title": "Preregistration when appropriate"}, {"id": "01d3ea69-d351-4e6c-b1b7-345ba001e65e", "type": "concept", "title": "Replication packages, codebooks, appendices, and audit trails"}, {"id": "5e22bc4c-3d11-4abe-bc4c-6cf87188216f", "type": "concept", "title": "Responsible openness for qualitative and sensitive data"}], "description": "Students learn current standards for credible social science."}]}, {"id": "0df0f25d-a3f5-449b-be3f-dc8635ee05ba", "type": "topic", "title": "Ethics, IRB, Community-Engaged Research, Equity, and Responsible Data Stewardship", "description": "This topic focuses on the moral and institutional obligations of sociological research, especially with vulnerable communities and sensitive data.", "children": [{"id": "583d0e0a-7d90-4c75-9750-faf482a73b26", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Human subjects ethics", "children": [{"id": "9809d66d-ba2e-48aa-b17b-42855aed6b68", "type": "concept", "title": "Informed consent, risk, benefit, deception, and debriefing"}, {"id": "02b4c19d-679c-463b-b464-30cec0bb3de1", "type": "concept", "title": "Privacy, confidentiality, anonymity, and identifiability"}, {"id": "36264a00-5415-4c4a-b05d-68468083ed01", "type": "concept", "title": "IRB review and exempt/expedited/full review logic"}], "description": "Students learn ethical duties before, during, and after data collection."}, {"id": "b7148a79-c19a-4cc5-9b03-e79590035880", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Community-engaged and participatory research", "children": [{"id": "ed38d729-1203-45e1-8a40-d91e91eb9cbd", "type": "concept", "title": "Stakeholder analysis and shared problem definition"}, {"id": "079f4631-1901-485a-8457-05f7371e8c03", "type": "concept", "title": "Reciprocity, co-production, and community advisory roles"}, {"id": "9a12c8ed-e7ec-4141-9aff-e65526472451", "type": "concept", "title": "Power, extraction, and benefit sharing"}], "description": "This subtopic centers research relationships and accountability."}, {"id": "dd6d00d6-2085-4a45-b16b-98f0cc60c676", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Responsible data stewardship", "children": [{"id": "6fe946d8-b071-4a42-a4ae-3eef26e9d77d", "type": "concept", "title": "Data management plans, storage, access, and retention"}, {"id": "8aa67008-1421-499e-a425-58ead03ccd3a", "type": "concept", "title": "De-identification, small-cell suppression, and sensitive data"}, {"id": "55c8563a-152c-42de-9fca-1e03007b6fcc", "type": "concept", "title": "Equity, bias, algorithmic harm, and data justice"}], "description": "Students learn to manage data securely and respectfully."}]}, {"id": "3e4de478-5c1f-49c2-aa24-7780e8a428a6", "type": "topic", "title": "Research Proposal, Methods Section, Presentation, and Capstone Study Design", "description": "The course culminates in a polished study proposal that integrates question, theory, design, data, ethics, analysis, and communication.", "children": [{"id": "91750b3a-012b-434e-94e9-90b77a109d9a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Proposal architecture", "children": [{"id": "9c1e9c09-7aa5-4660-b099-ac83d1c3de9e", "type": "concept", "title": "Problem statement, research question, literature, and conceptual framework"}, {"id": "5f00a1bd-56e3-4f87-8f4f-13f4e754ecdf", "type": "concept", "title": "Design, sample, data, measures, analysis, and limitations"}, {"id": "f1af6164-044b-461e-b6a9-7b1fd09c3b8a", "type": "concept", "title": "Timeline, feasibility, and ethics"}], "description": "Students bring the full course together in a feasible study design."}, {"id": "fae7fc5b-793d-4c9f-8bca-40177e2b38f5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Methods writing", "children": [{"id": "e1cc8281-069e-4674-b6db-7d1ceae32e59", "type": "concept", "title": "Participants/cases, data sources, instruments, procedures, and analysis plan"}, {"id": "02a0519c-5a96-4e4d-b02b-e0da9155858c", "type": "concept", "title": "Justification of design choices"}, {"id": "fd41343f-597c-4555-ae7e-1f2cd174119f", "type": "concept", "title": "Limitations and positionality statements"}], "description": "This subtopic teaches students to communicate procedures clearly enough for critique or replication."}, {"id": "5910e0da-dc53-4faa-8cdf-f02ac95c048d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Presentation and revision", "children": [{"id": "693b53ad-3f62-49ac-abca-4aeffae32517", "type": "concept", "title": "Peer review and design critique"}, {"id": "b65bdfc3-0026-40e9-b17c-83e9068d2b7f", "type": "concept", "title": "Conference-style presentation or poster"}, {"id": "6db00eb8-8d8d-4534-9aa1-4b4a4e9e273c", "type": "concept", "title": "Revision plan and capstone readiness"}], "description": "Students learn that research design improves through feedback, transparency, and iteration."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$srmjson$::jsonb,
